- `branch(b1)`, `branch(b2)`: Missing `guard` statements to enforce the explicit conditional logic ("If you are not hungry...", "If you are still not hungry..."); declared variables `v1` and `v2` are never referenced in any condition.
- `defines(v1, ...)`, `defines(v2, ...)`: Specify empty ranges `{}` instead of valid decision values (e.g., `{'Yes', 'No'}` or `{true, false}`), failing to model the binary nature of the hunger checks.
- `branch(b3, AND)`: Hallucinates parallel concurrency (AND gateway) that has no basis in the strictly sequential process description.
- `precedence(c1, n5)`: Violates source chronology by routing the initial shower path directly to "get on the bus", bypassing the mandatory second decision block ("If you are still not hungry...").
- `action(n5, "get on the bus")`, `action(n9, "get on the bus")`: Duplicates the final transportation step; the source text mentions "get on the bus" only once after all prior steps are complete.
- `action(n8, "have breakfast again")`: Modifies the exact source wording ("Otherwise, have breakfast.") by inserting the word "again".
- `precedence(b3, c1)`, `precedence(b3, n6)`: Creates concurrent branching after the first breakfast that contradicts the source's linear chronological order of checks and actions.

